@page "/legal/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy</PageTitle>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div class="mb-6 rounded-lg border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900 dark:border-amber-800 dark:bg-amber-950/40 dark:text-amber-200">
        <strong>Draft — not reviewed by a lawyer.</strong> This is placeholder boilerplate, not a legal
        document. Have it reviewed for your jurisdiction and actual business/data-handling specifics
        before relying on it.
    </div>

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><em>Last updated: [date]</em></p>

        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account data:</strong> name, email address, and (if you sign in that way) your Google/GitHub profile identifier.</li>
            <li><strong>Workspace content:</strong> issues, comments, attachments, and other content you or your workspace create.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> basic technical logs (e.g. sign-in times, error logs) needed to operate and secure the Service.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. How it's used</h2>
        <p>
            To operate the Service (authenticate you, show you your workspaces' data, send transactional
            email like password resets and invitations), and — only when you use those features — to send
            the text you provide to a third-party AI provider to generate a response.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Who can see your data</h2>
        <p>
            Data inside a workspace is visible to that workspace's members according to their role,
            enforced by the application. It is never shared with other workspaces or organizations.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Where it's stored</h2>
        <p>
            In a database and file storage operated for this Service. [Fill in: hosting location/provider,
            and object-storage provider if attachments are stored in an S3-compatible bucket rather than
            on the application server itself.]
        </p>

        <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            We use only the cookie needed to keep you signed in (a session/authentication cookie). We do
            not use third-party advertising or analytics cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Your choices</h2>
        <p>
            You can delete your account at any time from Account Settings, which removes your Identity
            record. If you are the sole admin of a workspace, you'll need to promote a co-admin or delete
            the workspace first. [Add: how to request an export or deletion of workspace-level data.]
        </p>

        <h2>7. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy: [contact email].</p>
    </article>
</div>
